# Resonance results worker (Bun + BullMQ)
#
# Consumes the `analysis-results` queue that apps/ml publishes to, and writes
# analyses / analysis_results / inference_runs. Run it with:
#   cd apps/worker && bun run dev

# --- Queue -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Same Redis as apps/api and apps/ml. Local: infra/docker/docker-compose.yml
REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379

# --- Database --------------------------------------------------------------
# The BYPASSRLS role, and this is the ONLY process that should hold it. Writing
# an ML result means writing rows for a user this process is not acting as, so
# it cannot go through withUser()/RLS the way a request can. Keep it out of
# apps/api/.env — that separation is the whole reason this is its own process.
APP_SERVICE_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://app_service.<ref>:<app-service-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true"

# --- Insights --------------------------------------------------------------
# Writes analysis_recommendations — the "do this" notes on the result screen.
# Every number (score, axes, timeline) is computed in code and does NOT need
# this key; leave it unset and analyses still complete, just without tips.
#
# Per-analysis cost is UNMEASURED — no real clip has run through this stage yet.
# It scales with transcript length and Opus 5 bills thinking tokens as output,
# so measure it on the first real batch instead of budgeting off a guess.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
